          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Angela Merkel's Early Years</strong><br>\nAngela Merkel was born in 1954 in Hamburg, West Germany, and moved with her family to East Germany as a child. She grew up in a politically controlled environment but focused on her education, excelling in mathematics and Russian, which paved the way for her future scientific career.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Education and Scientific Career</strong><br>\nMerkel pursued a career in science before entering politics. She earned a doctorate in physics from the University of Leipzig and worked as a research scientist specializing in quantum chemistry. Her scientific background influenced her analytical approach to politics later in her career.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Entry into Politics</strong><br>\nAfter the fall of the Berlin Wall, Merkel entered politics, joining the newly founded Democratic Awakening party. With the reunification of Germany, she became a member of the Christian Democratic Union (CDU) and quickly rose through its ranks, serving in various ministerial positions in the 1990s.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
