          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Merkel as the First Female Chancellor</strong><br>\nIn 2005, Angela Merkel made history by becoming Germany's first female Chancellor. She emerged as a leading figure in the CDU and won the chancellorship after the 2005 federal election. Merkel's election was a significant milestone for gender equality in German politics.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Merkel's Domestic Policies</strong><br>\nAs Chancellor, Merkel's domestic policy focused on social issues, economic reform, and environmental concerns. She promoted energy transformation towards renewable sources and enacted policies aimed at improving economic stability and growth while maintaining fiscal discipline.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Merkel and the European Union</strong><br>\nMerkel played a crucial role in the European Union, especially during financial crises. Her leadership was pivotal in navigating the Eurozone crisis, where she advocated for austerity measures and financial assistance for affected countries, balancing fiscal conservatism with European solidarity.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
