            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Merkel's Crisis Management</strong><br>\nMerkel's tenure as Chancellor saw several international crises, including the European migrant crisis in 2015. She made a landmark decision to open Germany's borders to refugees, a move that defined her humanitarian stance and was both praised and criticized domestically and internationally.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Stepping Down and Legacy</strong><br>\nAfter leading Germany for 16 years, Merkel decided not to seek re-election in 2021. She left office as one of the longest-serving leaders in Europe. Her pragmatic leadership style and her ability to compromise have left a lasting impact on German and European politics.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Merkel's Post-Chancellorship</strong><br>\nSince stepping down as Chancellor, Merkel has remained mostly out of the public eye, but her influence on global politics continues. She is respected for her leadership qualities and is often called upon for her expertise and perspective on current political issues.</p>\n"
              },
